  "quantity": "fGammaLavesConstituent is the fraction of the liquid that remains when the binary Scheil liquid reaches C_e = 18.9 wt% Nb (D96 Eq. 5); D96 treats it as the gamma/Laves eutectic-type constituent (eutectic gamma included) and compares it with volume %. It is not a phase fraction of Laves, and its phase identity is not established (see validity.phaseIdentityNote).",
  "quantityEnvelopeSchema": "metalliksa-quantity-envelope-1",
  "rapidSolidificationNote": "The k values below are equilibrium (weld/DTA) partition coefficients, so the fractions are upper bounds. A rapid-solidification estimate with solute trapping k(V) exists in the segregation block of a build job (LPBF Distortion Lab); it is not computed here.",
  "secondarySource": {
   "citation": "J.N. DuPont, 'Solidification of an Alloy 625 Weld Overlay', Metall. Mater. Trans. A 27A (1996) 3612-3620",
   "note": "full text (journal article, 9 pages) read for this module; one GMAW overlay of alloy 625 filler on 2.25Cr-1Mo steel at about 25-28 % dilution (Table II), plus a DTA sample of the same deposit",
   "read": true,
   "url": "https://www.osti.gov/biblio/413291"
  },
  "source": "Literature (weld and DTA studies: gas tungsten arc / GMAW welds and DTA samples), not LPBF; the numbers come from python/lpbf_solidification_segregation.py and are not a CALPHAD result",
  "status": "computed",
  "upperBoundNote": "Upper bound with respect to effects that are not modelled and that all reduce the terminal constituent: solid-state back-diffusion of Nb, solute trapping at high solidification rate, dendrite-tip undercooling, and Nb tied up as NbC by carbon (no carbon model for alloy 625). It is not a bound with respect to k_Nb or C_e. Against the C88 low-Fe measurements the estimate is high (see sourceAgreementNote), but that is one set of four heats at DTA cooling, not a guarantee.",
  "validity": {
   "ceTransferNote": "C_e = 18.9 wt% Nb is not measured on alloy 625: D96 (Section IV-C) builds it from Alloy 718 data (gamma 9.3 wt% Nb in the gamma/Laves eutectic, Table V) and the Fe-diluted overlay Laves (22.1 wt% Nb, Table III). C88 gives no eutectic composition; its Laves in low-Fe alloy 625 holds less Nb (16.8-19.2 wt%, Table V), so C_e for low-Fe IN625 may be lower, which would raise the computed fraction.",
   "d96SourceComposition_wt": {
    "C": 0.05,
    "Cr": 16.67,
    "Fe": 28.14,
    "Mo": 6.78,
    "Nb": 2.07,
    "Ni": 44.91,
    "Si": 0.24,
    "Ti": 0.17
   },
   "d96SourceNote": "D96 is a single Fe-diluted (28.14 wt% Fe) GMAW overlay (Table II); wrought and LPBF IN625 (Fe <= 5 wt%) are outside it, so its k_Nb is used only as a cross-check.",
   "kTransferNote": "k_Nb = 0.51 is the lowest of the four EPMA dendrite-core values in C88 Table VIII (0.51-0.53, alloys 5-8, Nb 3.53-3.61 wt%, Fe about 2.3 wt%); C88 Table VII gives 0.54 from liquidus/solidus slopes. The source Nb is 3.53-3.61 wt%, so the band ends (3.15 and 4.15 wt%) assume a constant k.",
   "outsideSourceComposition": true,
   "outsideSourceCompositionReasons": [
    "Fe: IN625 specification <= 5.0 wt% extends outside the source 2.26-2.31 wt%",
    "Cr: IN625 specification 20.0-23.0 wt% extends outside the source 21.65-21.83 wt%",
    "Mo: IN625 specification 8.0-10.0 wt% extends outside the source 9.67-9.81 wt%",
    "Nb: IN625 specification 3.15-4.15 wt% extends outside the source 3.53-3.61 wt%",
    "Si: IN625 specification <= 0.5 wt% extends outside the source 0.03-0.46 wt%",
    "C: IN625 specification <= 0.1 wt% extends outside the source 0.008-0.038 wt%",
    "Ti: IN625 specification <= 0.4 wt% extends outside the source 0.06 wt%",
    "Mn: IN625 specification <= 0.5 wt% extends outside the source 0.03 wt%"
   ],
   "outsideSourceRegime": true,
   "outsideSourceRegimeReason": "LPBF is not among the source processes (C88: GTA welds and DTA samples; D96: one GMAW overlay); k_Nb and the Scheil assumption were not established at LPBF solidification rates",
   "phaseIdentityNote": "Phase identity not established. In low-Fe alloy 625 (Fe about 2.3 wt%) C88 found the terminal constituent to depend on C and Si: with 0.038 wt% C and no added Si only gamma/NbC formed (alloy 6, no Laves); with low C and no added Si a small amount of mostly Laves formed (alloy 5); Si (0.38-0.46 wt%) promoted Laves and, at low C, M6C (Sections III-B and IV-B, Tables IV and IX). D96 adds that Fe favours Laves over NbC (Section IV-B). The IN625 specification allows C up to 0.10 and Si up to 0.50 wt%, so the computed number is a gamma/Laves-type estimate with C_e = 18.9 wt% Nb, not a Laves prediction; the constituent may be gamma/NbC, gamma/Laves or both.",
   "sourceAbsentElements": [],
   "sourceCompositionLocator": "C88 Table I, alloys 5-8 (Nb-bearing)",
   "sourceCompositionRange_wt": {
